Multiple Sequence Alignment using Multi Group Genetic Algorithm

1. machine environment
  [PIM version]
  Machine: PIM/m 256PEs
  SIMPOS : III Version 8.2
  PIMOS : 

  [KLICversion}
  Machine: Sparc Center (20PE)
  KLIC: Version 1.7

  [gavtool]
   Machine: Sparc
   SunOS: Release 4.1.3-JLE1.1.3 OS/AS=V4.13 (AB1405)
   System Memory: 16M
   DISK Memory: 10M
   Toolkit: OpenWare/Motif version2

2. how to install
   [PIM version]
   Please FTP the files under kl1 to your machine that is accessable to PIM/m.
   If you access to PIM by telnet, 'to UNIX file system' is O.K.
   (*.unload : binary mode
    *.kl1 & *.com : ascii mode)

   After login to PIM(PIMOS login),
   in "KL1 listener", please input;
 	> load("gav.unload"). [return]
   then KL1 program will be loaded on PIM.
   And when you input;
	> take "compile.com". [return]
   then you can re-compile KL1 source files.

   [KLIC version]
   Please FTP all files under software/gav/KLIC to your machine,
   that's have installen distributed KLIC system.
   Then please modify the source file main.kl1 like below;
  
   if internet address of your machine that do gavtool is A.B.C.D 
   then 
       old: {{192,156,144,116},10000},              % SocketAddress
       ->
       new: {{A,B,C,D},10000},              % SocketAddress

   After that please enter "compile" command.

   [gavtool]
   Please make same directory structure as directory "gav" on SUN machine.
   And on directory "gav", please input;
   	$ make
   then two files, gavtool/gavtool & gadmks/gadmks, will be made.
   And please copy gadmks into directory gavtool.

3. How to execute
   [PIM version]
   Example goal is written in "kl1/demo.com"
   After setting XENVIRONMENT "gav/gavtool/gavtool.res",
   please input;
	% gav/gavtool/gavtool
   then "Fitness Graph window" appears.
   Then in "Fitness Graph window" appears, please click "simulation"&"start"
   (Please check port No. = 10000.)
   After that, on KL1 listener, enter the goal.

   goal syntax is below;

   gav:ga(
	SeqList,	% Sequence List [List of string data]
	NameList,	% Name of Sequence's List [List of string data]
	GrpVectList,	% List of GrpVet, [List of Vector]
			% GrpVect = {Population,SelectionRate} [Vector of int]
	CrossoverRate,	% crossover percentage [integer]
	OneCycleTime,	% Time of one cycle (sec) [integer]
	DPCutRatio,	% Cut percentage in Dynamic Programming [integer]
	GapParam,	% GapCost Parameter  {A,B,C} (cost=A+B*K)
			% [vector of int]  
	ExecTime,	% Execution Time (sec) [integer]
	RandomSeed,	% Seed of Random Numbers [integer]
	Address,	% Internet address and port No. for gavtool [vector]
			% default port No. = 10000
			% 192.26.9.203 => {{192,26,9,203},10000}
	Output ).	% Output.

   [KLIC version]
   After setting XENVIRONMENT "gav/gavtool/gavtool.res",
   please input;
	% gav/gavtool/gavtool
   then "Fitness Graph window" appears.
   Then in "Fitness Graph window" appears, please click "simulation"&"start"
   (Please check port No. = 10000.)
   After that, please enter "gav" command on xterm.
   And if you change the data and/or parameters, 
   then please modify main.kl1 and "compile" again.
   Goal syntax is same as PIM version.

4. gavtool info 
[Fitness Graph window]
   To see real time display on KL1 program executuion, 
   before execution starts, click "simulation"&"start".
   If you use the already executed data file, please click "file"&"open",
   and decide the file to read.
   example data is "cross0.gatd" and "cross10.gatd" under gav/gavtool

   In this Fitness Graph window,
   we can see the real lines that is history of average fitness scores in
   each group and dotted lines that is history of maximum and minimum 
   scores.
   We can change the lines displayd by change "options"&"dislpay group"

   expand : giving the range by mouse right button
   shrink : giving the range by mouse center button
   (You can change the direction by click 
    "options"の"expand ..." and change it.)

   On this graph if we click mouse right button, 
   We can see "Individual Distribution graph window".

[Individual Distribution graph window]
    On this window, if we click the bar by mouse right button,
    we can see the individual informatin.
    (Individual ID, fitness score, last migration, last crossover)

    And on Individual Distribution graph window, if you click the Group
    Alphabet Character, you can see the best score alignment in the group.
